MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Another issue is that for inla, you're using E(prec)^-1 in the calculation of phy_inla, but in phy_brms, you're using E(std.dev <http://std.dev>)^2, which is not the same quantity unless there is no posterior uncertainty in the precision parameter.

Finn

